WEBVTT

00:00:03.980 --> 00:00:07.700
Why exactly is Sayuri-nee sitting at the table 
like it's the most natural thing in the world?

00:00:07.700 --> 00:00:10.640
Oh, it's fine, Tsu-kun!

00:00:11.690 --> 00:00:15.970
Well, she said she wanted to eat with us.

00:00:15.970 --> 00:00:18.330
Turning her away would be kinda... y'know?

00:00:18.330 --> 00:00:20.380
That's right, Tsurayuki-kun!

00:00:20.380 --> 00:00:24.030
We ought to be grateful to her!

00:00:25.720 --> 00:00:28.210
I guess you've all sold out for food, huh?

00:00:28.210 --> 00:00:29.380
Tsu-kun!

00:00:29.910 --> 00:00:31.710
Here. Say, "Ah!"

00:00:31.710 --> 00:00:33.540
That is not happening!

00:00:32.940 --> 00:00:35.550
<i>Tsurayuki's fiancée has suddenly shown up.</i>

00:00:33.540 --> 00:00:37.060
But I used to feed you 
like this all the time!

00:00:36.530 --> 00:00:40.580
<i>They're apparently childhood friends 
who promised to get married.</i>

00:00:37.900 --> 00:00:39.920
Now, say, "Ah!"

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.570
<i>Sayuri-san seems intent 
on winning Tsurayuki over,</i>

00:00:43.570 --> 00:00:46.810
<i>and ideally, bringing him 
back home with her.</i>

00:00:47.570 --> 00:00:48.600
Kyoya-kun!

00:00:49.950 --> 00:00:51.440
Here, say, "Ah!"

00:00:51.440 --> 00:00:53.150
Wait, why, "Ah"?

00:00:55.360 --> 00:00:56.520
Kyoya!

00:00:57.280 --> 00:01:00.120
You need to get some vegetables, too!

00:01:00.120 --> 00:01:02.410
Now, say, "Ah!"

00:01:02.410 --> 00:01:04.910
You seem to be having fun, Kyoya.

00:01:04.910 --> 00:01:07.500
I could say the same thing about you.

00:02:41.640 --> 00:02:43.220
Move up, move up!

00:02:44.020 --> 00:02:46.130
Sayuri-nee lived next door,

00:02:46.130 --> 00:02:48.600
and we've known each other 
since nursery school.

00:02:48.920 --> 00:02:54.250
Whenever my parents or siblings 
wouldn't pay attention to me,

00:02:54.250 --> 00:02:56.640
she was always there to take care of me.

00:02:56.640 --> 00:03:01.280
When I was really little, I used to 
think she was my actual older sister.

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:04.280
But she's your fiancée, right?

00:03:04.280 --> 00:03:07.370
That's something our parents decided 
without asking me. And it's stupid.

00:03:08.330 --> 00:03:11.040
I love Sayuri-nee as a person,

00:03:11.690 --> 00:03:14.350
but it's not anything more than that.

00:03:14.350 --> 00:03:16.090
That's why I ran.

00:03:16.680 --> 00:03:19.600
I didn't want to reject her outright, 
and hurt her feelings.

00:03:20.170 --> 00:03:21.510
I see.

00:03:21.510 --> 00:03:23.840
I feel bad for the rest of you, too.

00:03:23.840 --> 00:03:26.670
We were really getting rolling, 
and now this happens.

00:03:27.300 --> 00:03:29.620
I'll tell her to keep away from 
the house as much as possible.

00:03:29.620 --> 00:03:31.350
I wouldn't worry about it.

00:03:32.660 --> 00:03:35.240
I mean, she keeps bringing 
fancy ingredients by every time,

00:03:35.240 --> 00:03:37.720
which keeps both Shinoaki 
and Nanako in a good mood.

00:03:41.320 --> 00:03:42.860
<i>I said that, but...</i>

00:03:44.490 --> 00:03:48.550
<i>Sayuri-san visited 
the share house pretty regularly,</i>

00:03:48.550 --> 00:03:50.310
<i>and eventually every day.</i>

00:03:50.310 --> 00:03:54.030
<i>And by the time we had gotten used to it, 
it was time for winter vacation,</i>

00:03:54.410 --> 00:03:57.130
<i>which gave us more time 
to devote to game development.</i>

00:03:58.010 --> 00:03:59.840
Kyoya, could you check this?

00:03:59.840 --> 00:04:04.590
I did so many rewrites I didn't know
 what I was looking at anymore.

00:04:04.590 --> 00:04:06.770
So I scrapped it and redid it from scratch.

00:04:06.770 --> 00:04:08.700
Wait, the <i>whole</i> thing?!

00:04:08.700 --> 00:04:09.670
Yeah.

00:04:09.670 --> 00:04:13.980
This is what I came up with, 
after considering the style of bishoujo games.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:15.480
Does it work?

00:04:23.800 --> 00:04:25.460
This is amazing, Tsurayuki!

00:04:25.990 --> 00:04:28.860
The pacing of the dialog, 
the balance of the monologues...

00:04:28.860 --> 00:04:31.140
I knew you could do it. This is perfect.

00:04:31.140 --> 00:04:32.160
Really?

00:04:32.160 --> 00:04:34.370
Yeah. This script will work.

00:04:34.370 --> 00:04:35.370
We can do this!

00:04:38.070 --> 00:04:40.420
Thank goodness...

00:04:40.420 --> 00:04:43.200
Now I can get some real sleep!

00:04:43.920 --> 00:04:47.530
Okay, that takes care of the script.

00:04:47.530 --> 00:04:50.800
Yamashina-san's been sending 
in the backgrounds on time,

00:04:51.090 --> 00:04:52.310
so that just leaves...

00:04:55.350 --> 00:04:58.210
Kyoya, help!

00:04:59.870 --> 00:05:04.700
I just don't think I can do this. 
Composing something out of the blue...

00:05:08.040 --> 00:05:09.000
What's this?

00:05:09.320 --> 00:05:12.750
A melody came to mind, 
so I stuck it in there...

00:05:13.160 --> 00:05:16.620
It's nowhere near good enough 
to be music, though.

00:05:17.370 --> 00:05:18.840
You already did it.

00:05:20.560 --> 00:05:22.390
Wait, is that good enough?

00:05:22.390 --> 00:05:25.600
What about arrangements 
or coming up with a longer version?

00:05:25.600 --> 00:05:29.570
It's okay. That's what 
the music software is for.

00:05:29.570 --> 00:05:31.110
Once we have a good melody,

00:05:31.110 --> 00:05:34.040
we can come up with a few 
loops to make it longer,

00:05:34.040 --> 00:05:36.910
and changing the arrangement 
won't be hard at all.

00:05:38.760 --> 00:05:40.080
I'm so relieved.

00:05:40.080 --> 00:05:42.440
Na... Nanako?

00:05:42.820 --> 00:05:47.520
Don't. Just let me recharge a little.

00:05:47.920 --> 00:05:50.880
<i>Uh, Nanako, I don't know if...</i>

00:05:52.870 --> 00:05:55.150
Okay! I'm recharged!

00:06:00.220 --> 00:06:01.280
Thanks!

00:06:01.280 --> 00:06:03.250
I'm feeling better now,
 so I'll be able to get back to work!

00:06:06.640 --> 00:06:07.510
Okay.

00:06:16.620 --> 00:06:17.810
<i>Does she...</i>

00:06:18.750 --> 00:06:20.730
<i>Nah, I have to be overthinking it.</i>

00:06:20.730 --> 00:06:22.110
Kyoya-kun?

00:06:22.110 --> 00:06:23.210
Something wrong?

00:06:23.210 --> 00:06:26.050
Oh, nothing! It's nothing.

00:06:26.050 --> 00:06:27.400
Anyway, what do you think?

00:06:27.880 --> 00:06:30.800
I think his art's real impressive!

00:06:30.800 --> 00:06:31.950
That's good.

00:06:32.440 --> 00:06:35.450
It hit me when I was checking out 
the exhibition during the school festival.

00:06:35.450 --> 00:06:40.290
Yamashina-san's backgrounds 
would be a good match for your art.

00:06:40.810 --> 00:06:42.290
<i>I knew Shinoaki could do it,</i>

00:06:42.290 --> 00:06:44.760
<i>considering she's going to be 
Akishima Shino some day.</i>

00:06:45.160 --> 00:06:47.920
<i>The art needed to be different 
from her usual style,</i>

00:06:47.920 --> 00:06:51.140
<i>and she managed to meet 
the challenge in hardly any time at all.</i>

00:06:51.140 --> 00:06:53.480
I gotta ask, Kyoya-kun...

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:54.670
What is it?

00:06:55.940 --> 00:06:58.100
What's going on in this scene?

00:06:58.100 --> 00:07:00.140
Th-That's...

00:07:03.960 --> 00:07:05.150
A sex scene.

00:07:05.150 --> 00:07:08.570
I don't mean that, I just dunno 
what they're doing.

00:07:08.570 --> 00:07:10.420
What they're... what?

00:07:10.420 --> 00:07:13.970
I know! Kyoya-kun, could you sit over there?

00:07:18.790 --> 00:07:20.130
Sh-Shinoaki?!

00:07:20.130 --> 00:07:22.500
Don't move, now! Stay put.

00:07:24.360 --> 00:07:27.130
It gets this big, huh?

00:07:27.130 --> 00:07:28.920
Wh-What does, exactly?!

00:07:28.920 --> 00:07:30.470
The thighs.

00:07:31.810 --> 00:07:34.600
Oh... the thighs. Right.

00:07:34.600 --> 00:07:37.260
And it goes up right here...

00:07:38.250 --> 00:07:41.270
How'm I supposed to sketch like that?

00:07:43.520 --> 00:07:46.270
Come on over, now!

00:07:46.270 --> 00:07:49.700
Eek!

00:07:50.780 --> 00:07:53.660
Here's the additional script 
and some of the art files.

00:07:53.980 --> 00:07:58.230
I was worried when I heard the plan 
was to make a game in four months...

00:07:58.230 --> 00:08:00.750
But I'm glad things seem 
to be going smoothly.

00:08:00.750 --> 00:08:02.790
I don't know if I'd go that far.

00:08:02.790 --> 00:08:05.050
Even with school on break, 
we've still got work,

00:08:05.050 --> 00:08:07.130
so everyone's worn out.

00:08:09.000 --> 00:08:10.740
Wh-What is it?

00:08:10.740 --> 00:08:14.060
I was curious what kind 
of trick you used this time.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:14.930
Trick?

00:08:15.210 --> 00:08:19.600
For this. Rokuonji's script, 
Shinoaki's illustrations...

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:22.000
They're well done, sure,

00:08:22.000 --> 00:08:25.420
but it's all pretty distinct 
from their usual style.

00:08:26.680 --> 00:08:30.370
Yeah. We need to make sure 
it sells well, so...

00:08:30.370 --> 00:08:33.360
I asked them to go for something 
a bit more commercial.

00:08:34.530 --> 00:08:37.200
You just... asked?

00:08:37.200 --> 00:08:38.270
Yeah...

00:08:38.270 --> 00:08:40.200
This is why you freak me out!

00:08:41.780 --> 00:08:43.520
Shinoaki is one thing,

00:08:43.520 --> 00:08:47.200
but do you realize how remarkable it is 
to convince Rokuonji to change his style,

00:08:47.200 --> 00:08:48.750
just so it'd be more popular?

00:08:50.240 --> 00:08:52.120
He must really trust you.

00:08:52.800 --> 00:08:54.880
The fact that you can do that...

00:08:55.280 --> 00:08:57.750
I hate to admit it, 
but I'm seriously impressed.

00:08:58.260 --> 00:09:01.440
Something about you makes 
others put their faith in you.

00:09:01.440 --> 00:09:04.410
"Whatever Hashiba says is probably true."

00:09:04.860 --> 00:09:06.240
Kawasegawa...

00:09:06.560 --> 00:09:10.720
A-Anyway, if you're seriously doing this, 
make sure it turns out well!

00:09:22.730 --> 00:09:25.420
It's already the end of the year, huh?

00:09:31.320 --> 00:09:33.180
It's so cold!

00:09:33.180 --> 00:09:37.260
Winters in Fukuoka are pretty dang cold, 
and this is about as cold as that.

00:09:38.490 --> 00:09:40.180
Yeah.

00:09:40.510 --> 00:09:43.220
Do you want to get something warm to drink?

00:09:43.220 --> 00:09:45.560
Naw, I'm okay.

00:09:45.560 --> 00:09:48.310
Oh, can we go to the art supply store?

00:09:48.770 --> 00:09:49.980
Of course.

00:09:49.980 --> 00:09:53.980
<b>ABE'S ELECTRONICS</b>

00:09:50.640 --> 00:09:53.230
Sorry for dragging you along 
on my shopping trip.

00:09:53.230 --> 00:09:53.980
It's okay.

00:09:53.980 --> 00:09:57.570
The idea of being out here by myself
 today was kind of depressing.

00:09:57.570 --> 00:09:59.870
I'm glad you came with me, Shinoaki.

00:10:01.320 --> 00:10:02.230
Yeah?

00:10:03.300 --> 00:10:05.330
Well, all right, then.

00:10:09.380 --> 00:10:12.080
Still... you sure you're okay 
with it being me?

00:10:14.150 --> 00:10:17.010
It's Christmas Eve, y'know?

00:10:22.640 --> 00:10:23.820
Sorry.

00:10:24.520 --> 00:10:26.520
That was a funny thing to ask.

00:10:34.500 --> 00:10:37.030
<i>New Year's came, and it's now 2007.</i>

00:10:39.530 --> 00:10:42.280
That was such a huge crowd!

00:10:42.280 --> 00:10:44.690
What'd you ask for, Kyoya-kun?

00:10:44.690 --> 00:10:48.000
You have to ask? For the game 
to get finished and sell well!

00:10:48.300 --> 00:10:51.960
I seriously hope it sells... 
for all our sakes.

00:10:51.960 --> 00:10:55.680
And for Tsurayuki, who has finally learned 
to show concern for other people!

00:10:55.680 --> 00:10:56.920
Listen, you...

00:10:56.920 --> 00:11:01.320
Oh, come to think of it, vocal talent, 
did you finish the opening song?

00:11:01.320 --> 00:11:03.270
What is "vocal talent" supposed to mean?!

00:11:03.270 --> 00:11:05.170
I'm looking forward to it, y'know!

00:11:05.170 --> 00:11:06.700
Considering you canceled your plans

00:11:06.700 --> 00:11:09.390
for going to the special 
Christmas Eve sale with Kyoya—

00:11:09.390 --> 00:11:12.430
Wh-What are you even talking about?!

00:11:12.430 --> 00:11:13.650
Nanako?

00:11:15.270 --> 00:11:18.110
U-Uh... well...

00:11:18.110 --> 00:11:22.260
Since we're all out anyway, let's grab 
something to eat before we head home.

00:11:22.260 --> 00:11:24.120
G-Good idea!

00:11:24.120 --> 00:11:25.760
Sounds good! I'm in.

00:11:25.760 --> 00:11:28.080
Yeah, let's get some food, Kyoya!

00:11:29.680 --> 00:11:31.580
Yeah, I think so.

00:11:33.920 --> 00:11:35.960
<i>Though there was the occasional surprise,</i>

00:11:35.960 --> 00:11:39.250
<i>we were steadily making 
progress on our game.</i>

00:11:46.250 --> 00:11:48.920
It really turned into a game!

00:11:48.920 --> 00:11:51.610
This is only partway through 
the first scene, though.

00:11:51.610 --> 00:11:55.330
But... I think even just this little bit 
is enough to get me emotional.

00:11:55.330 --> 00:11:58.610
You can save the tears 
for after you play through my story!

00:11:59.930 --> 00:12:02.610
<i>The game goes on sale on April 29th.</i>

00:12:03.160 --> 00:12:06.490
<i>Even if we're on schedule,
 we'll still be pressed for time.</i>

00:12:06.920 --> 00:12:09.920
<i>My job is to guide everyone 
until the deadline hits,</i>

00:12:09.920 --> 00:12:11.500
<i>and make sure the game sells well.</i>

00:12:12.050 --> 00:12:14.510
<i>I'm not making the same 
mistakes I did ten years ago.</i>

00:12:14.970 --> 00:12:18.250
<i>I'm going to make sure 
the remake of my life is a success!</i>

00:12:18.930 --> 00:12:21.120
Tsurayuki, can I—

00:12:21.120 --> 00:12:23.260
Hey, Tsu-kun...

00:12:23.260 --> 00:12:27.190
I know work is important, 
but can't we relax some?

00:12:27.190 --> 00:12:28.210
Come on...

00:12:28.210 --> 00:12:31.200
Sayuri-nee, I'm begging you, 
not when I'm writing.

00:12:31.200 --> 00:12:33.250
What's this, then?

00:12:33.250 --> 00:12:38.070
"Akiya-kun, look at what 
you've done to me..."

00:12:38.710 --> 00:12:40.980
"So don't tease me any more, okay?"

00:12:42.650 --> 00:12:44.130
Please stop!

00:12:46.070 --> 00:12:49.490
You think about pervy stuff 
like this, huh, Tsu-kun?

00:12:49.490 --> 00:12:51.600
No! This is just work!

00:12:51.600 --> 00:12:52.610
It's fine.

00:12:52.610 --> 00:12:56.380
We can do everything that 
you've written about, y'know?

00:12:56.380 --> 00:12:58.720
U-Um... Sayuri-san?

00:12:59.640 --> 00:13:01.090
Oh, did you need something?

00:13:01.560 --> 00:13:03.420
<i>This is kinda pushing it.</i>

00:13:04.730 --> 00:13:06.840
What should I do?

00:13:06.840 --> 00:13:08.260
I know what you mean.

00:13:08.260 --> 00:13:12.520
I'm frankly impressed Tsurayuki was 
able to say no in spite of all that.

00:13:12.820 --> 00:13:16.350
This is unrelated, but... you two...

00:13:16.690 --> 00:13:20.050
Is there a reason why you're 
both sitting next to me?

00:13:20.050 --> 00:13:22.530
You sure you're not imagining things?

00:13:22.530 --> 00:13:25.390
I reckon you're thinking too hard 
about it, Kyoya-kun.

00:13:25.390 --> 00:13:27.340
But this is...

00:13:30.640 --> 00:13:32.250
Thank you! Come again!

00:13:34.180 --> 00:13:35.700
Hey, what's wrong?

00:13:37.610 --> 00:13:39.130
You've been spacing out.

00:13:39.130 --> 00:13:41.090
N-No! It's nothing!

00:13:43.270 --> 00:13:47.040
Come to think of it, you were in Shinoaki's 
room all day yesterday, weren't you?

00:13:47.590 --> 00:13:49.730
What were you two doing?

00:13:49.730 --> 00:13:52.930
What do you mean? I was checking the CG.

00:13:53.370 --> 00:13:58.400
She also asked me to take 
a few pictures for reference.

00:13:58.400 --> 00:14:00.550
And that was really it?

00:14:00.550 --> 00:14:01.930
Of course!

00:14:01.930 --> 00:14:05.650
Oh, I had better go restock the drinks!

00:14:11.120 --> 00:14:12.580
This is bad.

00:14:13.050 --> 00:14:17.920
There's a chance this could 
affect the game's production.

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.460
I'll help.

00:14:21.460 --> 00:14:24.460
We did this before, huh?

00:14:24.460 --> 00:14:26.090
Y-Yeah...

00:14:26.690 --> 00:14:28.940
It was a coincidence that time, but...

00:14:28.940 --> 00:14:30.930
But not today.

00:14:31.800 --> 00:14:33.310
I'm doing it on purpose, okay?

00:14:43.940 --> 00:14:45.030
Nanako...

00:14:45.600 --> 00:14:46.850
I won't lose.

00:14:50.950 --> 00:14:55.460
<i>I don't think there's any 
other way to interpret this.</i>

00:14:56.540 --> 00:14:58.040
What are you, stupid?!

00:14:58.040 --> 00:15:00.600
Why the hell would you ask me about this?!

00:15:00.600 --> 00:15:02.480
L-Look, I'm sorry!

00:15:03.270 --> 00:15:09.160
I m-mean, I guess as a member of 
Team Kitayama, I can't just ignore it.

00:15:09.160 --> 00:15:10.270
Yeah.

00:15:10.270 --> 00:15:13.010
Well? Which one of them
 do you like, Hashiba?

00:15:13.010 --> 00:15:15.250
What do you mean?

00:15:15.250 --> 00:15:19.180
They're both great girls, but I don't 
really feel that way about either of them.

00:15:20.550 --> 00:15:23.340
And yet, instead of actually just saying no,

00:15:23.340 --> 00:15:27.030
you keep up this wishy-washy noncommittal
attitude, leading us to this point.

00:15:27.030 --> 00:15:28.070
Does that cover it?

00:15:28.070 --> 00:15:29.820
It does, ma'am.

00:15:29.820 --> 00:15:32.950
From a woman's perspective, 
that makes you a total dirt bag!

00:15:32.950 --> 00:15:35.240
...is what I would say ordinarily.

00:15:35.780 --> 00:15:38.090
But considering your position 
from a production standpoint,

00:15:38.090 --> 00:15:41.250
I understand why you've 
done things this way.

00:15:41.250 --> 00:15:44.960
I think, for the time being, you'll have to 
continue pretending to be oblivious.

00:15:45.340 --> 00:15:48.000
Other than that, avoid being alone 
with either of them in a closed room,

00:15:48.000 --> 00:15:51.160
and steer conversations away 
from the subject.

00:15:51.990 --> 00:15:54.000
Sadly, that's all I can really offer.

00:15:54.570 --> 00:15:57.180
Sorry I couldn't be more help.

00:15:57.180 --> 00:15:58.780
That's not true.

00:15:59.680 --> 00:16:02.690
I feel a little better just 
getting to talk about it.

00:16:03.060 --> 00:16:05.630
I knew I could count on you, Kawasegawa.

00:16:07.310 --> 00:16:11.350
Well, when you finish the project, 
you need to make clear how you feel.

00:16:11.350 --> 00:16:13.720
That's the least you can do for them.

00:16:13.720 --> 00:16:15.660
Okay. Thanks again!

00:16:21.400 --> 00:16:24.000
Seriously, is he stupid?

00:16:26.120 --> 00:16:28.550
You think this part might 
be a little too forceful?

00:16:28.550 --> 00:16:34.150
I get what you mean, but I don't 
want to compromise here.

00:16:34.150 --> 00:16:37.690
It's the climax of the story, where the 
protagonist chooses the girl he likes.

00:16:37.690 --> 00:16:39.720
That seems like it's a pretty 
intense situation, right?

00:16:39.720 --> 00:16:41.270
The thing is, most players will decide

00:16:41.270 --> 00:16:43.720
based on how they feel 
about the character's quirks.

00:16:43.720 --> 00:16:46.280
And when you consider that, 
I think we've done a great job

00:16:46.280 --> 00:16:48.440
of showcasing those aspects of them.

00:16:49.580 --> 00:16:50.570
Still, man...

00:16:50.570 --> 00:16:53.720
Tsu-kun! You're coming home 
with me today, right?

00:16:53.720 --> 00:16:56.950
Sayuri-nee, this is really important!

00:16:57.850 --> 00:17:00.760
I think Tsu-kun's a little exhausted.

00:17:01.290 --> 00:17:04.700
Kyoya-san, could you discuss this later?

00:17:04.700 --> 00:17:06.440
Well, I—

00:17:06.440 --> 00:17:07.750
Come on, Tsu-kun.

00:17:09.620 --> 00:17:14.350
Your mother and father 
are really worried about you.

00:17:14.350 --> 00:17:15.740
You should come—

00:17:15.060 --> 00:17:18.390
Dad would never say that.

00:17:18.390 --> 00:17:20.560
That's not true! I'm sure he—

00:17:20.560 --> 00:17:21.970
I know he wouldn't!

00:17:27.220 --> 00:17:30.320
I think I'll excuse myself for today.

00:17:33.640 --> 00:17:34.740
I'm sorry.

00:17:38.810 --> 00:17:42.710
Sorry... I know I'm behind schedule,
 and now this...

00:17:42.710 --> 00:17:44.120
It's not your fault.

00:17:44.550 --> 00:17:46.460
You should take the rest of the day off.

00:17:46.460 --> 00:17:49.580
But isn't my stuff late already?

00:17:49.580 --> 00:17:51.850
I don't want you working like this, anyway.

00:17:51.850 --> 00:17:53.530
I'll manage something.

00:17:54.500 --> 00:17:55.170
Kyoya...

00:17:56.840 --> 00:18:00.300
You're amazing, man. I really respect you.

00:18:01.840 --> 00:18:05.060
Don't be ridiculous. 
Just make sure to rest up.

00:18:05.060 --> 00:18:05.950
Okay.

00:18:10.010 --> 00:18:13.730
<i>After that day, Sayuri-san stopped
 dropping by the house.</i>

00:18:14.290 --> 00:18:17.850
<i>In the following week, 
the share house was more quiet,</i>

00:18:17.850 --> 00:18:20.120
<i>but also a little bit more lonely.</i>

00:18:27.790 --> 00:18:30.790
C-Can I help you?!

00:18:34.340 --> 00:18:35.850
Hashiba Kyoya-san...

00:18:36.290 --> 00:18:39.270
I'm sorry, but can I have 
a moment of your time?

00:18:43.520 --> 00:18:45.270
This is a lovely view.

00:18:45.270 --> 00:18:47.270
I-I think so, too.

00:18:47.860 --> 00:18:53.330
<i>Something about this gives me a real 
"You'll be sleeping with the fishes!" vibe...</i>

00:18:55.340 --> 00:18:59.560
What did you need to talk 
to me about in a place like this?

00:19:02.300 --> 00:19:04.790
If you want to threaten me about Tsurayuki,

00:19:04.790 --> 00:19:06.940
you're wasting your time. I—

00:19:06.940 --> 00:19:08.880
What are you talking about?

00:19:09.750 --> 00:19:13.410
There was something 
I wanted to discuss with you

00:19:13.410 --> 00:19:14.960
which is why I brought you here.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:18.090
I'm going home tomorrow.

00:19:19.480 --> 00:19:20.820
I've realized something.

00:19:21.260 --> 00:19:27.090
At this rate, Tsu-kun won't return 
to me, or to his parents.

00:19:27.580 --> 00:19:33.230
But before I left, there was something 
 I needed to confirm with you.

00:19:33.230 --> 00:19:34.190
With me?

00:19:34.880 --> 00:19:38.610
All Tsu-kun seems to talk 
about lately is you.

00:19:38.610 --> 00:19:43.450
"Kyoya is amazing. If I rely on him, 
things will turn out fine."

00:19:44.080 --> 00:19:46.110
Which is why I would like to ask...

00:19:46.800 --> 00:19:50.870
What kind of relationship 
do the two of you have?

00:19:52.040 --> 00:19:54.040
To be specific, is there a physical—

00:19:54.040 --> 00:19:55.890
No, no, no, no!

00:19:55.890 --> 00:19:57.700
Why would you think there was?!

00:19:57.700 --> 00:19:59.730
Really? I'm surprised.

00:20:00.170 --> 00:20:02.650
Considering the depth of his trust in you,

00:20:02.650 --> 00:20:05.870
I expected there to be 
an intimate element to it.

00:20:07.720 --> 00:20:09.720
Putting that aside, though,

00:20:10.180 --> 00:20:14.450
what exactly are your plans 
for your relationship with Tsu-kun?

00:20:15.830 --> 00:20:18.420
He's a son of the Rokuonji family.

00:20:18.420 --> 00:20:21.860
If he returns home, a stable future 
is promised him.

00:20:22.500 --> 00:20:28.250
And yet you all seem to be dragging 
Tsu-kun down a riskier path.

00:20:29.510 --> 00:20:32.480
Can you make any 
guarantees about his future?

00:20:32.480 --> 00:20:34.370
Do you think that's right?

00:20:36.500 --> 00:20:38.340
I can't make any promises.

00:20:38.960 --> 00:20:40.610
I'd imagine not.

00:20:40.610 --> 00:20:43.490
In that case, you should tell him—

00:20:42.470 --> 00:20:46.390
But this is a path that 
Tsurayuki chose for himself.

00:20:47.240 --> 00:20:49.250
He chose it, fully aware of
 the risks it carries.

00:20:50.340 --> 00:20:53.140
Which is why I want to support him.

00:20:53.490 --> 00:20:56.150
And if that makes him happy...

00:20:56.670 --> 00:20:59.820
Then I want to be there 
to celebrate his choice.

00:21:00.810 --> 00:21:04.240
Do you think Tsu-kun is happy, then?

00:21:04.580 --> 00:21:06.620
He's honestly in a bit of trouble.

00:21:06.620 --> 00:21:10.190
But that's why we intend to make 
a game based around his writing,

00:21:10.190 --> 00:21:12.370
and sell it in order to help him 
get out of that trouble.

00:21:12.660 --> 00:21:16.830
That indecent story? 
Does that kind of thing really sell?

00:21:17.230 --> 00:21:18.750
There's a good chance it will.

00:21:18.750 --> 00:21:21.430
I wouldn't have suggested it, otherwise.

00:21:21.430 --> 00:21:24.400
We're making a product 
that's on a competitive level.

00:21:24.400 --> 00:21:25.720
I'm proud of that fact.

00:21:28.280 --> 00:21:29.970
I understand.

00:21:29.970 --> 00:21:33.310
It's not that I believe everything you say,

00:21:33.310 --> 00:21:35.830
but I understand the passion 
and resolve that you have.

00:21:35.830 --> 00:21:37.470
Thank you.

00:21:39.840 --> 00:21:44.390
Please... help Tsu-kun find happiness.

00:21:55.210 --> 00:21:58.960
This was for the best, right, Tsurayuki?

00:22:00.100 --> 00:22:03.720
To help you reach 
a future where you're happy.
